WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:04.060
A lot of us ain’t got enough sense to get out of here.

2
00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:06.080
But hey, God going to take us out of there.

3
00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:10.600
He blessed us in a way indirectly.

4
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.520
Here’s your chance.

5
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:16.200
Your blessings come to you in all different kind of ways.

6
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:23.660
It’s just up to you be able to accept them, and go ahead on with them and make something good out of it.

7
00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:30.180
And I think this is . . . that Sasol and its buyout is good.

8
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:41.920
Because I’ve been through . . . first one with PPG that we had property down in Bayou d’Inde and we sold.

9
00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.220
That was the first company that started the buyouts?

10
00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:48.640
With me, with my family.

11
00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:49.060
Okay?

12
00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:57.380
With the Lee family was down on the bayou,

13
00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:07.420
south of Mossville there on the south side of Highway 90, we had a 200-acre strip in there.

14
00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:16.520
In the beginning, my grandfather inherited it from his dad and his mother.

15
00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:22.340
Some industry, support industry bought portions of it.

16
00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:27.280
PPG, Jupiter Chemical, bought some of it.

17
00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:32.120
It enabled me to build my house in Mossville.

18
00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:37.520
And then from there . . . I called it a blessing then.

19
00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:43.540
And from there, Conoco bought my house in Mossville.

20
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:43.740
Okay?

21
00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:46.000
A blessing, you understand?

22
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.160
Bought my land.

23
00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:51.100
Then my mother died and we had some property,

24
00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:59.220
me and my brother had some property together in Mossville by my mother’s house and then now Sasol bought that,

25
00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:03.080
me and my brother’s land and my mother’s land.

26
00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:04.140
Okay?

27
00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.000
Blessing, okay?

28
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:11.980
My grandparents and them had land there in Mossville, and the Lemelles.

29
00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:15.840
And Sasol, we in the process of selling that now.

30
00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:17.120
Blessing again.

31
00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:22.260
I thank God every morning, because I say, man, that’s five or six times.

32
00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:31.560
And then my Grandmother Lee, when we moved from Bayou d’Inde, bought some property there in Mossville and we moved the house.

33
00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:35.420
We tore the house down, but we still have the property.

34
00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:37.380
So bam, that’s another Lee.

35
00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:38.540
You know what I’m saying?

36
00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:43.880
And I say wow, I mean, if people can’t see that. [*] They say, “Well, we’re not you.”

37
00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:49.700
Well, I guess not, you know, but you’re still getting some kind of blessing out of it.

38
00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:52.140
You’re getting a chance to get out of there.

39
00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:56.660
You all been hollering about moving and this and that, and this and that,

40
00:02:56.660 --> 00:03:00.580
and they’re giving you three and four times the value of your property.

41
00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:01.620
That’s a blessing.
